  "about": {
    "description": "USDO is a rebasing yield-bearing USD stablecoin issued by OpenEden Digital, a Bermuda Monetary Authority DABA-licensed segregated accounts company. It maintains a target 1 dollar redemption value and is fully backed by tokenized short-dated US Treasury bills through the OpenEden TBILL product line. Yield from the underlying Treasury portfolio accrues to holders via positive rebases of the token balance rather than a rising unit price. USDO is deployed as an EIP-1967 upgradeable ERC-20 on Ethereum, Base, BSC, and Kaia and as a Solana Token-2022 mint with transferHook and metadata extensions. A separate ERC-4626 wrapper called cUSDO offers non-rebasing DeFi composability by tokenizing USDO shares that accrue value through a rising convertToAssets rate. Continuous proof of reserves is published through Chainlink Proof of Reserve feeds and OpenEden transparency reporting.",
